{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514029-how-much-can-a-mortal-occultist-know-about-the-abyss","id":1514029,"title":"How much can a mortal occultist know about the abyss?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-06T11:35:56-07:00","id":1514029,"title":"How much can a mortal occultist know about the abyss?","content":"I am starting a character, newly embraced into clan lasombra, 4 dots in occult.<br /> <br /> Id kinda like to impress fellow Lasombra with theorycrafting about the abyss, that said i am not sure how much a mortal could have learned about it.<br /> <br /> Technicly speaking there is mortal sources, like the cabalistic tree of life and its dark side with daath being the crossing from one to the other, or ancient religions that worshipped darkness and the cold, many mystical implementations of meditating in darkness, sensory depravation leading to all kinds of experiences, and even in christianity it is mentioned that there was only darkness, before the light.<br /> <br /> Mortal infernalists are a thing too and i guess demons can tell about the abyss and someone surely wrote it down. I am not sure if any kainite book could have found its way into mortal hands or how much the inquisition may or may not know about the abyss.<br /> <br /> Obviously i dont want him to have practical knowledge or actually traversing the abyss as mortal, just how much theoretical knowledge could he have?<br /> <br /> i am also not sure how many abyss related hedge sorcery rituals and spells exist that dont require vitae to use","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T11:48:04-07:00","id":1514033,"title":"","content":"There's like 20+ places called the abyss I think there's lots of room for missunderstandings. <br /> <br /> But I don't see why a Lasombra couldn't just start a cult and give mortals the information as part of the religion. Rule through terror. There are some powers that would greatly assist in doing that. Maybe some (un)lucky fellow gets embraced after some time in that cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T12:37:28-07:00","id":1514036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514029-how-much-can-a-mortal-occultist-know-about-the-abyss?p=1514033#post1514033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some powers that would greatly assist in doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>May i ask to elaborate on that? it sounds like a great idea ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T23:55:52-07:00","id":1514085,"title":"","content":"Allaborate a bit please ^^<br /> The Abyss which lies between the Supernal World and the Fallen World in Mage: The Awakening?<br /> The Abyss from which the Lasombra gain their powers of Obtenebration in Vampire: The Masquerade?<br /> The Abyss in which the Fallen were trapped until the Reckoning in Demon: The Fallen?<br /> The Abyss which is a Realm in the Near or Middle Umbra in Werewolf: The Apocalypse?<br /> The Abyss, as a term that Les Invisibles use for the Tempest in Wraith: The Oblivion?<br /> <br /> Sure, some overlaps... a bit<br /> But since you mentioned Lasombra?<br /> A Human - if have proper sources - could have as much knowledge as a vampire (or anything really) - usually this ends up either in an Embrace or a murder<br /> So yeah, it is totally plausible, a Lasombra &quot;groom&quot; a cult, share knowledge to further her experiments and studies, since - tho once a vampire was a human - a human can see things differently, another point of view<br /> It is a bit like those logic of a child experiments, when they present a problem to a kid, and with simple logic it solves it with a method the grown ups forgot basically<br /> ...or when in Starate: SG-1 the Asgardian asked the Humans help against the Replicators becasue they were so advanced basically forgot to think... dumb and violently<br /> A bit same here<br /> A fresh point of view could mean a brakethrugh<br /> And humans are clever... give them proper background and sources and they are capable of anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T00:20:20-07:00","id":1514087,"title":"","content":"Interesting question assuming the obtenerbration lasombra Abyss I'd suggest very little. Unlike hell or the near umbra the Abyss doesn't really interact with our world until the lasombra summon it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T00:29:30-07:00","id":1514089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514029-how-much-can-a-mortal-occultist-know-about-the-abyss?p=1514036#post1514036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> May i ask to elaborate on that? it sounds like a great idea ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>1:Obtenebration alone is a spectacular display.<br /> 2: You'll probably have Dominate, and you can set conditions for mesmerize. &quot;If you leave the town's borders, return here&quot; &quot;if you talk to the police, try to kill them&quot; &quot;if you defect, kill your kids&quot; Now sure, you can only apply one mesmorize to a person and can't get them to kill themselves, <b><i>but they don't know that</i></b>. Once you get Dominate 4 you can use it like a punishment to intimidate folks (and get some enforcers too) <br /> 3:There's a few combo disciplines. You can dominate through shadows, you can give someone the impression that shadows are after them. <br /> 4: Magic. Abyss mysticism or thaumaturgy. Convince people the shadows are watching them, or you can find anything if you ask. Simple, low level rituals like Thaumaturgy rituals like bind the accusing tongue work wonders, and powers like brand don't have any effect but can still be used creatively to terrorize the hell out of someone. <br /> <br /> Other disciplines. Presence is obvious, Potence is great for showing off, Animalism can do a lot in terms of fear; the animals are watching you and report to me, do as I say or you'll end up like that... Auspex lets you read minds. Mask of a thousand faces is one of the best abilities for messing with someone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T00:52:47-07:00","id":1514093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514029-how-much-can-a-mortal-occultist-know-about-the-abyss?p=1514087#post1514087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting question assuming the obtenerbration lasombra Abyss I'd suggest very little. Unlike hell or the near umbra the Abyss doesn't really interact with our world until the lasombra summon it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be a nice source of a Mortal game tho'<br /> Myths are filled with shadows (even Peter Pan had a living shadow...)<br /> Just to name a few, the <b>Nalusa Falaya</b> is a creature from Choctaw mythology. Its name is literally translated to &quot;long black being&quot;\u200b, it is a shadow creature that resembled a man with slanted eyes and pointy ears. It would approach men on its belly like a snake. He would frighten hunters at night.<br /> In Greek mythology <b>Erebus </b>(&quot;deep darkness, shadow&quot;), or Erebos, is the personification of darkness and one of the primordial deities<br /> In Ancient Rome, the shadow was called the umbra. After a person died their shadow went to the Land of the Shades which was a part of the Underworld. This part of the underworld was for people who were not heroes. They stayed in that part of the underworld as a shadow figures<br /> A <b>shadow person</b> (also known as a <b>shadow figure</b>, <b>shadow being</b> or <b>black mass</b>) is the perception of a patch of shadow as a living, humanoid figure, particularly as interpreted by believers in the paranormal or supernatural as the presence of a spirit or other entity.\u200b<br /> The Coast to Coast AM late night radio talk show helped popularize modern beliefs in shadow people. The first time the topic of shadow people was discussed at length on the show was April 12, 2001 when host Art Bell interviewed Native American elder Thunder Strikes, who is also known as Harley &quot;SwiftDeer&quot; Reagan. During the show, listeners were encouraged to submit drawings of shadow people that they had seen and a large number of these drawings were immediately shared publicly on the website. In October that year, Heidi Hollis published her first book on the topic of shadow people, and later became a regular guest on Coast to Coast. Hollis describes shadow people as dark silhouettes with human shapes and profiles that flicker in and out of peripheral vision, and claims that people have reported the figures attempting to &quot;jump on their chest and choke them&quot;.<br /> Even the <b>Slender Man </b>could be listed here with a bit of a stretch <br /> <br /> These could be potential manifestations of the Abyss and a Human could devote her life to study these and since it is the World of Darkness, these myths even could be real and could find... <i>something </i>(usually something with fangs and a strange diet)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T01:18:06-07:00","id":1514094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514029-how-much-can-a-mortal-occultist-know-about-the-abyss?p=1514085#post1514085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allaborate a bit please ^^<br /> The Abyss which lies between the Supernal World and the Fallen World in Mage: The Awakening?<br /> The Abyss from which the Lasombra gain their powers of Obtenebration in Vampire: The Masquerade?<br /> The Abyss in which the Fallen were trapped until the Reckoning in Demon: The Fallen?<br /> The Abyss which is a Realm in the Near or Middle Umbra in Werewolf: The Apocalypse?<br /> The Abyss, as a term that Les Invisibles use for the Tempest in Wraith: The Oblivion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since im going to be a Lasombra i meant the Abyss that spawns obtenebration and Lasombra Abyss mystics call upon.<br /> <br /> that said i dont see ho this couldnt be the same abyss that traps the demons as they are angelic beings created by god into the light so casting them into the abyss older than the light would be a severe punishment and would cause sensory depravtion and stuff demons describe to suffer there<br /> <br /> Also great input so far =) I guess some lovecraftian lore could also be used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T01:53:05-07:00","id":1514096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514029-how-much-can-a-mortal-occultist-know-about-the-abyss?p=1514094#post1514094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that said i dont see ho this couldnt be the same abyss that traps the demons as they are angelic beings created by god into the light so casting them into the abyss older than the light would be a severe punishment and would cause sensory depravtion and stuff demons describe to suffer there</div> </div> </div> </div>With a very complicated way, but could work<br /> Demon: The Fallen have actually two abysses (abyssi?)<br /> On is described as the Infinite Nothing, less than Nothing, everything that is not God and the Elohim created the physical space and the whole Creation to seperate God infinity from tha Abyss' absolute nothingess<br /> The other is the murky dimension of darkness created by the victorious Host as an eternal prison for the Fallen. It is located beneath the Underworld, featureless, dark, cold, windy and empty - it is closer to sensory deprivation than to anything else... and it is as close to the &quot;real&quot; Abyss as it could get, some material even describes it the Abyss, the prison itself is at the edge of the Abyss, the abolsute Nothing and darkness that co-existed with God, the total abscence of God Infinity<br /> The Abyss of the Umbra is the equivalent to a spiritual black hole, the Abyss is surrounded by thick mists, leading to a realm of barren mud and rocks. This in turn leads to the gaping pit that is so deep and wide that it must be bottomless. Anything tossed into the Abyss is forever lost, simply disappearing as though they never existed. Almost anything that has fallen into the Abyss has <i>never</i> come back out again\u200b. This realm devours all forms of sensory perception, wither they come from light, sound or even scent. If is foolish enough to go far enough, there is the threat of complete sensory deprivation. At that point however, they are lost for all times.<br /> The center of the Abyss could be the mouth of the Wyrm, and could lead to Oblivion and/or the Abyss of the Fallen.<br /> The Lasombra's/Vampire Abyss is seemingly empty of native inhabitants, the realm itself is quasi-sentient, and will sometimes display physical or mental manifestations. Such manifestations can be summoned into the material world by high-level mastery of both Obtenebration and Shadow Occultism, but several sources about Abyss misticism describes the Abyss as the Darkness before God commanded, let it be Light - the primodial Nothingess - witch is actually could be the Abyss from the Elohim shaped Creation<br /> May cainite scholars belive, Vicissitude and Obtenebration are actually the manifestation of their respective Qliphoth, realities with different laws of physics than our own - you can interpret that, the Qliphoth of Obtenebration is actually the Abyss that co-existed with God, the absolute nothing, wich tainted the Elohim and Creation, and where the Prison of the Fallen of the same name located, at the very edge, and that edge is basically the very maw of the Wyrm, Oblivion itself<br /> <br /> Would gives a funny twist to any Fallen game where they encounter a Lasombra... \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T02:09:55-07:00","id":1514097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1514029-how-much-can-a-mortal-occultist-know-about-the-abyss?p=1514096#post1514096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Would gives a funny twist to any Fallen game where they encounter a Lasombra... \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>As in demions finally fearing a kindred for their command over the very realm they fear, maybe able to have sjhadow tentacles drag them back into their prison or, as it has life and light leeching effects, maybe even destroy the demon for good if engulfed in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T02:21:52-07:00","id":1514098,"title":"","content":"Basically<br /> Just immagine, you are a Fallen, escaped from There and the only thing is keeping the Prison to suck you back is your new flesh suit, the mortal body you moved in, evicting the previous owner if it not left already<br /> Then the spawn of the First Murderer, whos deed ended the Age of Wrath first part, the &quot;silent war&quot; (fought as one-on-one duels between loyalists and rebels. These duels took place on abstract levels of reality and were not fatal or even particularly violent; once it became clear that one angel would inevitably win, both sides would withdraw and acknowledge the victor.) and the Age of Wrath took a darker turn. The rebel angels and the Elohim learned how to kill and were willing to do it (both human and angelic) and ultimately led to the Time of Atrocities, the Babel Project and the Shattering and thus the the Sebettu lost the War... <br /> ...this cursed undead <i>thing </i>summons the very power that wants you back... even the low Shroud of Night that blanket an area in a cloud of unnatural shadow that obscures light, sound, and heat, it could be maddeding, even tho' it is not totall sensory depravtion could be horrific reminder of the Prison<br /> Even to a Sebettu, the Darkness that is from prior creation could be frightening - and could trigger PTSD<br /> Would you risk - uppon witnessing the Darkness coming alive, consuming light, sound, heat and with tentacles reaching toward you and sensing its hunger - it is something that actually could pull you back to the Prison you managed to escape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}